- Offline-mode feature REVERTED per user ("undo all offline feature", "we will work later").
  - Deleted `app/components/button/OfflineButton.js` + `app/utils/offline.js`.
  - Removed `useOfflineSongs` from SongsList, HorizontalSongs, SongExplorer, ShowAll n/w,
    SearchMore, Favorited, Playlist, GenreSong, Songs, RandomButton.
  - Removed `<OfflineButton/>` from Album, Artist, Genre, Favorited, Playlist headers.
  - Dropped `isOffline` from `defaultSettings` + "Offline" key from en.json.
  - All those files byte-identical to HEAD again. Kept unrelated in-progress work
    (queue DnD, playlist sort/swipe, server switch, Favorited home song section 17b).
- eslint clean; release APK rebuilt + installed on R5CY71GYKWF.
- Committed + pushed.
- **Silent caching downloads** (commit `a95c31f`): cache-ahead `downloadNextSong` enqueues with
  `silent: true`; `DownloadBanner` and the per-song `%`/clock indicators in `SongItem` skip silent
  items (via `getSongState`), so auto-caching runs invisibly. Manual downloads still animate.
- **Long download queue lag** (commit `1210f86`): with ~1000 queued items the O(n) scans were the
  problem, not tick frequency. (a) id→item `queueById` map rebuilt once in `setState`, used by
  `getSongState`/`onProgress`/`moveToQueue` → O(1) lookups; (b) `Settings/Downloads` screen renders
  the active-queue rows with `LegendList` (virtualized, only visible rows mounted) instead of
  `.map()`-ing 1000 rows into a ScrollView — static sections moved to `ListHeaderComponent`/
  `ListFooterComponent`.
- **Parallel downloads** (commit `4de25e8`): replaced the single-slot `isProcessing` boolean with an
  `activeDownloads` counter; `startNext()` fills up to N slots concurrently. N = new
  `parallelDownloads` setting (default 3), editable under **Settings → Downloads → Song caching**
  ("Parallel downloads", integer input next to "Cache next song"). Pause/cancel/clear correctly
  release slots (cancel only decrements when the item had a live resumable). i18n en/de.
- Shared-song semantics confirmed (no code change): songs in 2+ downloaded collections accumulate
  sources on the index entry; `removeSource` deletes the file only when sources drop to `[]`, so
  deleting one playlist keeps the shared song for the other. Known edge case (deferred): deleting a
  collection while a shared song is still queued cancels that queue item and it won't re-download
  for the surviving collection.

